                        <seg type="rubrication">Divine names; three pairs of lines on the incipit page of <ref target="#ms_i1"/> alternating with black lines; the initial line in the
                           beginnings of sections of <ref target="#ms_i1"/> and <ref target="#ms_i2"/>; two initial lines on the incipit
                           page of <ref target="#ms_i2"/>; corrections written interlineally (e.g., <locus target="#12v #18r #37v"/>); 
                           elements of punctuation signs; the word <foreign xml:lang="am">kǝfǝl</foreign> ‘part’; elements
                           of Ethiopic numerals; some other words, e.g., <foreign xml:lang="gez">wangel</foreign> ‘gospel’ (<locus target="#15v #17v #30r"/>, 
                           <foreign xml:lang="gez">ʾOrit</foreign>, ‘Pentateuch’ (<locus target="#25r #48v"/>), <foreign xml:lang="gez">dǝrsān</foreign> ‘homily’ (<locus target="#66v"/>), 
